{"name":"Boston Legacy","hex":"#685043","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"legacy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Money or property bequeathed to someone in a will.","Something inherited from a predecessor or the past."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Left over from the past; old and no longer current.English Wikipedia has an article on:Legacy systemWikipedia","Belonging to a class of boardgame where permanent changes are made to game elements such as the board, cards and rules over multiple play sessions."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/legacy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Boston Legacy FC","blocks":[{"text":"Boston Legacy FC is an American professional soccer team based in the Greater Boston area that competes in the National Women's Soccer League (NWSL). Joining in 2026, its home ground will be at a renovated White Stadium, though the club plays at Gillette Stadium in Foxborough, Massachusetts, and Centreville Bank Stadium in Pawtucket, Rhode Island, during the team's first two seasons while White Stadium is redeveloped."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/ab/Boston_Legacy_FC.svg/330px-Boston_Legacy_FC.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boston_Legacy_FC","wikidata":"Q124322952"},{"title":"Boston","blocks":[{"text":"Boston is the capital and most populous city of the U.S. state of Massachusetts. It serves as a cultural and financial center of New England, a region of the Northeastern United States. Boston has an area of 48.4 square miles (125 km2) and a population of 675,647 as of the 2020 census, making it the third-most populous city in the Northeastern United States after New York City and Philadelphia. The larger Greater Boston metropolitan statistical area had a population of 5 million in 2025, making it the largest metropolis in New England and the eleventh-largest in the United States."}],"image":"ht